The runs graft `tm-oracle plan` applies AFTER `plan-seam.patch` (stage 6 W-40 land
step; the owner's D74, parity P64, README gap 3740).  `build-oracle.sh` applies it
with `git apply` and FAILS the build when it does not apply.

Fork 4748911's §8.2 step 5 splits a §7.5 batch by `loc:`, splittability and the
running block with a GROUP-BY (`split_by_filters`: a member joins the FIRST bucket
with its key, wherever that bucket sits).  The owner's D74 splits it into RUNS (a
member joins the LAST bucket when it carries that bucket's key, else opens a new
one) — the kernel's `Planner.splitPush`.  This graft adds that split behind an
opt-in, `PlanInput::with_runs`, which the oracle sets when a request carries
`"runs": true` (the comparand's departure for P64, as `order` is D60's); a request
without it plans the fork's group-by, byte for byte as before.  The in-tree fork
(`tm-core/src/planner.rs`) carries the same opt-in, which `tm/src` never sets.

